title: "AI Safety: a practical toolkit and knowledge base for safe LLM deployment"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AdilShamim8/AI-Safety"
abstract: >-
  A combined documentation library, Python toolkit, and benchmark-harness
  collection for AI safety. Covers alignment techniques (RLHF, DPO,
  Constitutional AI), interpretability, LLM risk taxonomies (prompt injection,
  jailbreaks, hallucination, bias, privacy), governance frameworks (NIST AI
  RMF, EU AI Act, OWASP LLM Top 10), and red-teaming methodology. All
  benchmark harnesses target real public datasets: TruthfulQA, GSM8K, MMLU,
  BBQ, BOLD, ToxiGen, RealToxicityPrompts, AdvBench, XSTest, HH-RLHF,
  BeaverTails, and JailbreakBench.
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - llm-alignment
  - guardrails
  - prompt-injection
  - red-teaming
  - responsible-ai
type: software
